WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.738
Welcome back to your Danish citizenship exam companion.

2
00:00:03.688 --> 00:00:09.024
This is Chapter Six, Episode Five: the Danish flag, and the royal house.

3
00:00:09.574 --> 00:00:14.586
The Danish national flag, Dannebrog, is a white cross on a red background.

4
00:00:14.536 --> 00:00:19.074
Dannebrog means "the Danes' banner" or "the red-coloured banner".

5
00:00:19.074 --> 00:00:35.154
Even though the legend tells that Dannebrog fell down from the sky during a military battle in Estonia in 1219 and secured the Danes the victory, the flag is in reality probably a banner that was already used by the knights who went on crusades in the Middle Ages.

6
00:00:35.704 --> 00:00:45.166
Dannebrog is regarded as one of the world's oldest national flags and has since the 1400s been used as a banner when Danish kings went to war.

7
00:00:45.117 --> 00:00:52.992
Through the 1600s and 1700s, it was only the authorities and the navy that used the Danish national flag.

8
00:00:52.992 --> 00:00:58.841
But from the middle of the 1800s, it became popular among the population to fly the flag.

9
00:00:58.841 --> 00:01:06.216
Today many Danes fly Dannebrog on festive occasions, for example a private birthday or an official day of observance.

10
00:01:06.216 --> 00:01:14.172
The flag is also used at funerals, where the flag is only raised halfway up the flagpole until the funeral has taken place.

11
00:01:14.722 --> 00:01:18.647
On certain dates all public authorities must fly the flag.

12
00:01:18.597 --> 00:01:24.484
They must for example do so at church festivals, and when members of the royal family have birthdays.

13
00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:29.160
Many companies and private persons also mark these days by raising Dannebrog.

14
00:01:29.159 --> 00:01:33.260
Historical days of observance are also marked by flying Dannebrog.

15
00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:42.486
This applies, for example, to Denmark's liberation on the fifth of May, and Constitution Day, grundlovsdag, on the fifth of June.

16
00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:49.099
In Denmark it is not allowed to fly other countries' flags than the Danish without permission from the police.

17
00:01:49.049 --> 00:02:00.792
You may, however, fly the flag of Greenland, the flag of the Faroe Islands, the other Nordic countries' flags, and the UN flag and the EU flag without the police's permission.

18
00:02:01.342 --> 00:02:09.305
Denmark's best-known order, a medal, the Order of the Dannebrog, Dannebrogordenen, is named after the Danish flag.

19
00:02:09.255 --> 00:02:21.522
It is awarded by the king to senior civil servants, politicians, cultural figures, military people, prominent business people and researchers who have made a special effort to promote Denmark's interests.

20
00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:25.071
Now, the royal house, Kongehuset.

21
00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:30.696
The Danish royal house is among the oldest of the world's total of 43 monarchies.

22
00:02:30.696 --> 00:02:36.946
It is over a thousand years old and can with certainty be traced back to Gorm den Gamle in the 900s.

23
00:02:36.946 --> 00:02:44.496
From and including him, Denmark has had a total of 54 monarchs: 52 kings and two queens.

24
00:02:45.046 --> 00:02:56.608
From 1448 to 1863, Denmark was ruled by the Oldenburg family, and afterwards by the Glücksburg family, which has the same ancestors as the Oldenburgs.

25
00:02:56.558 --> 00:03:03.646
Denmark's present monarch is King Frederik the Tenth, born 1968, who belongs to this family.

26
00:03:03.646 --> 00:03:18.446
He succeeded his mother Queen Margrethe the Second, who chose to abdicate on the fourteenth of January 2024, the same date in 1972 on which she herself took over the throne at her father Frederik the Ninth's death.

27
00:03:18.446 --> 00:03:29.082
Since 1448, when the Oldenburg family took over the throne, 20 of 21 Danish kings have, by the way, been called either Christian or Frederik.

28
00:03:29.632 --> 00:03:32.269
Denmark is a constitutional monarchy.

29
00:03:32.219 --> 00:03:37.419
That means the monarchy works within the framework of the constitution and democracy.

30
00:03:37.419 --> 00:03:43.519
The monarch, the king or queen, is not politically elected, but inherits the throne.

31
00:03:43.519 --> 00:03:46.257
The king has no real political power.

32
00:03:46.257 --> 00:03:54.969
He does not interfere in political life, does not express political views and cannot, conversely, be held responsible for the government.

33
00:03:54.969 --> 00:03:59.657
A number of the king's formal tasks are however connected to political life.

34
00:03:59.657 --> 00:04:09.804
He takes part, among other things, in the opening of the Folketing on the first Tuesday of October and takes part when ministers are to be appointed or a new government formed.

35
00:04:10.354 --> 00:04:16.641
The king signs the laws passed by the Folketing and the government together with the politically responsible minister.

36
00:04:16.591 --> 00:04:24.486
This takes place at the Council of State, statsråd, at Christiansborg, where the king meets with the government's ministers.

37
00:04:25.036 --> 00:04:31.673
The king is also host when Denmark receives state visits, and he represents the country at state visits abroad.

38
00:04:31.623 --> 00:04:37.512
The king also carries out a long series of other formal and representative tasks in Denmark.

39
00:04:38.062 --> 00:04:41.774
The king and the royal house are a national rallying point.

40
00:04:41.724 --> 00:04:47.574
The royal house has a central place in Danes' history and is very popular among the population.

41
00:04:47.574 --> 00:05:02.549
Many follow, for example on TV, when the monarch on New Year's Eve gives his traditional speech from the royal family's home at Amalienborg in Copenhagen or from the residence at Fredensborg Palace, Fredensborg Slot, outside Copenhagen.

42
00:05:02.549 --> 00:05:09.837
Amalienborg is the royal family's home; Christiansborg is where the Council of State, statsråd, meets.

43
00:05:09.837 --> 00:05:17.130
And many turn up at Amalienborg Palace Square and cheer the king on his birthday, which is the 26th of May.

44
00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:25.467
The king has since 2004 been married to Queen Mary, born 1972, who originally comes from Australia.

45
00:05:25.417 --> 00:05:38.992
Together they have four children: Crown Prince Christian, born 2005, Princess Isabella, born 2007, and the twins Prince Vincent and Princess Josephine, born 2011.

46
00:05:38.992 --> 00:05:45.300
The eldest, Crown Prince Christian, will one day take over the throne as Christian the Eleventh.

47
00:05:45.868 --> 00:05:48.218
Here is your recap for Episode Five.

48
00:05:48.168 --> 00:05:54.981
Dannebrog is a white cross on a red background and means "the Danes' banner" or "the red-coloured banner".

49
00:05:54.981 --> 00:05:59.231
The legend says it fell from the sky in Estonia in 1219.

50
00:05:59.231 --> 00:06:06.568
It is regarded as one of the world's oldest national flags and has been used as a royal banner since the 1400s.

51
00:06:06.568 --> 00:06:09.956
At funerals the flag is flown at half mast.

52
00:06:09.956 --> 00:06:18.318
Without police permission you may only fly the flags of Greenland, the Faroe Islands, the Nordic countries, the UN and the EU.

53
00:06:18.318 --> 00:06:21.918
The Order of the Dannebrog is Denmark's best-known order.

54
00:06:21.918 --> 00:06:30.181
The Danish royal house is among the oldest of the world's 43 monarchies, traceable to Gorm den Gamle in the 900s.

55
00:06:30.181 --> 00:06:34.806
Denmark has had 54 monarchs, 52 kings and two queens.

56
00:06:34.806 --> 00:06:40.293
The Oldenburgs ruled 1448 to 1863, then the Glücksburgs.

57
00:06:40.293 --> 00:06:50.443
King Frederik the Tenth, born 1968, succeeded his mother Margrethe the Second, who abdicated on the fourteenth of January 2024.

58
00:06:50.443 --> 00:06:53.293
The king's birthday is the 26th of May.

59
00:06:53.293 --> 00:07:05.793
On nytårsaften, New Year's Eve, the monarch, today the king, gives the traditional speech to the whole realm; older exams say the queen; it is not Christmas Eve or Constitution Day.

60
00:07:05.793 --> 00:07:12.331
Liberation Day, the fifth of May, and Constitution Day, the fifth of June, are both flag days.

61
00:07:12.331 --> 00:07:21.120
He has been married to Queen Mary, from Australia, since 2004, and they have four children, with Crown Prince Christian the eldest.

62
00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:24.270
Now it is time for your exam practice.

63
00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:29.132
These are real questions from past Danish citizenship exams on what you just heard.

64
00:07:29.132 --> 00:07:36.618
For each one, I will read the question and the choices, then pause so you can pick your answer, and then I will give you the correct answer.

65
00:07:37.168 --> 00:07:38.418
Question 1.

66
00:07:38.368 --> 00:07:42.643
